An elected official accused of violations of the code of ethics shall be entitled to due process, which shall include:
(1) To representation by counsel of his choice at his expense at all stages of these proceedings;
(2) To written notice of any complaints or charges filed against him;
(3) To copies of all pleadings filed in a case against him;
(4) To at least ten (10) days notice prior to any hearing held by the hearing officer under this article; and
(5) To cross-examine witnesses and to call witnesses and otherwise present evidence in his defense at a hearing, unless the complaint is dismissed upon initial review by the hearing officer.
(Ord. No. 380, § 1(attch.), 10-7-14)

